0	section	Standard dialogue
0	section	Initial dialogue
1	line	Wise Old Man	Greetings, {player}.
1	line	Player	So you're a wise old man, huh?
1	line	Wise Old Man	Less of the 'old' man, if you please!
1	line	Wise Old Man	But yes, I suppose you could say that. I prefer to think of myself as a sage.
1	line	Player	So what's a sage doing here?
1	line	Wise Old Man	I've spent most of my life studying this world in which we live. I've strode through the depths of the deadliest dungeons, roamed the murky jungles of Karamja, meditated on the glories of Saradomin on Entrana,
1	line	Wise Old Man	and read some dusty tomes in the Library of Varrock.
1	line	Wise Old Man	Now I'm not as young as I used to be, I'm settling here where it's peaceful.
1	cond	If the player has not completed Vampyre Slayer:
2	line	Wise Old Man	It's a pity about that vampyre that keeps attacking the village. At least Saradomin protects me.
2	action	continue
1	line	Player	That's quite an exciting life you've had.
1	line	Wise Old Man	Exciting? Yes, I suppose so.
1	line	Wise Old Man	Now I'm here, perhaps I could offer you the benefit of my experience and wisdom?
1	line	Player	Thanks! So you can help me?
1	line	Wise Old Man	Well, I imagine you've gathered up quite a lot of stuff on your travels. Things you used for quests a long time ago that you don't need now.
1	line	Wise Old Man	If you like, I can look through your bank and see if there's anything you can chuck away.
1	line	Wise Old Man	Alternatively, you can bring items here and show them to me. If I see that it's something you don't need, I'll let you know. I might even be willing to buy it.
1	line	Player	So you'll help me clear junk out of my bank?
1	line	Wise Old Man	Yes, that's right. Or I'd be happy to chat with you about the wonders of this world!
1	option	Could I have some free stuff, please?
2	line	Player	Could I have some free stuff, please?
2	line	Wise Old Man	Deary deary me...
2	cond	If the player is in a F2P world:
