2	option	I'd just like to ask you something.
3	line	Player	I'd just like to ask you something.
3	line	Wise Old Man	Please do!
3	option	Distant lands
4	option	The Wilderness
5	line	Player	Could you tell me about the Wilderness, please?
5	line	Wise Old Man	If Entrana is a land dedicated to the glory of Saradomin, the Wilderness is surely the land of Zamorak.
5	line	Wise Old Man	It's a dangerous place, where adventurers such as yourself may attack each other, using all their combat skills in the struggle for survival.
5	line	Wise Old Man	The Wilderness has different levels. In a low level area, you can only fight adventurers whose combat level is close to yours.
5	line	Wise Old Man	But if you venture into the high level areas in the far north, you can be attacked by adventurers who are significantly stronger than you.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Of course, you'd be able to attack considerably weaker people too, so it can be worth the risk.
5	line	Wise Old Man	If you dare to go to the far north-west of the Wilderness, there's a building called the Mage Arena where you can learn to summon the power of Saradomin himself!
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	line	Player	Yes please.
6	option	Distant lands
7	action	above
6	option	Strange beasts
7	action	below
6	option	Days gone by
7	action	below
6	option	Gods and demons
7	action	below
6	option	Something to do with you...
7	action	below
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	line	Player	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	line	Wise Old Man	As you wish. Farewell, {player}.
6	action	end
4	option	Misty jungles
5	line	Player	What can you tell me about jungles?
5	line	Wise Old Man	If it's jungle you want, look no further than the southern regions of Karamja.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Once you get south of Brimhaven, the whole island is pretty much covered in exotic trees, creepers and shrubs.
5	line	Wise Old Man	There's a small settlement called Tai Bwo Wannai Village in the middle of the island. It's a funny place; the chieftain's an unfriendly chap and his sons are barking mad.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Honestly, one of them asked me to stuff a dead monkey with seaweed so he could EAT it!
5	cond	If the player has completed Tai Bwo Wannai Trio:
6	line	Player	Yes, I've met them.
6	action	continue
5	line	Wise Old Man	Further south you'll find Shilo Village. It's been under attack by terrifying zombies in recent months, if my sources are correct.
5	cond	If the player has completed Shilo Village:
6	line	Player	I've dealt with them, although there are a few still knocking about.
6	action	continue
5	line	Wise Old Man	The jungle's filled with nasty creatures. There are vicious spiders that you can hardly see before they try to bite your legs off, and great big jungle ogres.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
4	option	Underground domains
5	line	Player	Tell me about what's underground.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Oh, the dwarven realms?
5	line	Wise Old Man	Yes, there was a time, back in the Fourth Age, when we humans wouldn't have been able to venture underground. That was before we had magic; the dwarves were quite a threat.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Still, it's much more friendly now. You can visit the vast dwarven mine if you like; the entrance is on the mountain north of Falador.
5	line	Wise Old Man	If you go further west you may be able to visit the dwarven city of Keldagrim. But they were a bit cautious about letting humans in, last time I asked.
5	line	Wise Old Man	On the other hand, if you go west of Brimhaven, you'll find a huge underground labyrinth full of giants, demons, dogs and dragons to fight. It's even bigger than the caves under Taverley, although the Taverley
5	line	Wise Old Man	dungeon's pretty good for training your combat skills.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
4	option	Mystical realms
5	line	Player	What mystical realms can I visit?
5	line	Wise Old Man	Well, you've been to Zanaris. I met a fairy years ago who said she lived there. She was an incredible warrior, considering that she wasn't even a metre tall.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Also, in my research I came across ancient references to some kind of Abyss. Demons from the Abyss have already escaped into this land; Saradomin be thanked that they are very rare!
5	cond	If the player has completed Shadow of the Storm:
6	line	Player	I've been through a portal into the lair of some ancient demon. It was in the city of Uzer.
6	line	Wise Old Man	Ah, Uzer. A city much favoured by Saradomin, destroyed by Thammaron, the elder-demon, late in the Third Age.
6	line	Player	Yeah, there isn't much left there.
6	action	continue
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
3	option	Strange beasts
4	option	Biggest & Baddest
5	line	Player	What's the biggest monster in the world?
5	line	Wise Old Man	There's a mighty fire-breathing dragon living underground in the deep Wilderness, known as the King Black Dragon. It's a fearsome beast, with a breath that can poison you, freeze you to the ground or
5	line	Wise Old Man	incinerate you where you stand.
5	line	Wise Old Man	But even more deadly is the Queen of the Kalphites. As if her giant mandibles of death were not enough, she also throws her spines at her foes with deadly force. She can even cast rudimentary spells.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Some dark power must be protecting her, for she can block attacks using prayer just as humans do.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Another beast that's worthy of a special mention is the Shaikahan. It dwells in the eastern reaches of Karamja, and is almost impossible to kill except with specially prepared weapons.
5	cond	If the player has completed Tai Bwo Wannai Trio:
6	line	Player	Actually, that one's dead. I've been helping a barmy hunter who'd sworn to kill it.
6	action	continue
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
4	option	Poison and how to survive it
5	line	Player	What does poison do?
5	line	Wise Old Man	Many monsters use poison against their foes. If you get poisoned, you will not feel it at the time, but later you will begin to suffer its effects, and your life will drain slowly from you.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Over time the effects dwindle to nothing, but if you had already been wounded you might die before they wear off completely.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Fortunately, followers of Guthix have devised potions that can cure the poison or even give immunity to it.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Should you wish to use poison against your own enemies and those of our Lord Saradomin, there is a potion that you can smear on your daggers, arrows, spears, javelins and throwing knives.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
4	option	Wealth through slaughter
5	line	Player	What monsters drop good items?
5	line	Wise Old Man	As a general rule, tougher monsters drop more valuable items. But even a lowly hobgoblin can drop valuable gems; it just does this extremely rarely.
5	line	Wise Old Man	If you can persuade the Slayer Masters to train you as a Slayer, you will be able to fight certain monsters that drop valuable items far more often.
5	line	Wise Old Man	You might care to invest in an enchanted dragonstone ring. These are said to make a monster drop its most valuable items a little more often.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
4	option	Random events
5	line	Player	What are these strange monsters that keep appearing out of nowhere and attacking me when I'm training?
5	line	Wise Old Man	Ah, I imagine you see a lot of those.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Creatures such as the rock golem, river troll and tree spirit dwell in places where adventurers frequently go to train their skills. While you're training you will often disturb one by accident. It will then get angry and
5	line	Wise Old Man	attack you. The safest way to deal with them is to run away immediately, but they sometimes drop valuable items if you kill them.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
3	option	Days gone by
4	option	Heroic figures
5	line	Player	Tell me about valiant heroes!
5	line	Wise Old Man	Ha ha ha... There are plenty of heroes. Always have been, always will be, until the fall of the world.
5	cond	If the player has less than 80 quest points:
6	line	Wise Old Man	If you'd do a few more quests, you'd soon become a fairly noted adventurer yourself.
6	action	continue
5	cond	If the player has 80 or more quest points:
6	line	Wise Old Man	You're quite a noted adventurer yourself!
6	action	continue
5	line	Wise Old Man	But I suppose I could tell you of a couple...
5	line	Wise Old Man	Yes, there was a man called Arrav. No-one knew where he came from, but he was a fearsome fighter, a skillful hunter and a remarkable farmer. He lived in the ancient settlement of Avarrocka, defending it from
5	line	Wise Old Man	goblins, until he went forth in search of some strange artefact long desired by the dreaded Mahjarrat.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Perhaps some day I shall be able to tell you what became of him.
5	line	Wise Old Man	But do not let your head be turned by heroics. Randas was another great man, but he let himself be beguiled into turning to serve Zamorak, and they say he is now a mindless creature deep in the Underground Pass that
5	line	Wise Old Man	leads to Isafdar.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
4	option	The origin of magic
5	line	Player	Where did humans learn to use magic?
5	line	Wise Old Man	Ah, that was quite a discovery! It revolutionised our way of life and jolted us into this Fifth Age of the world.
5	line	Wise Old Man	They say a traveller in the north discovered the key, although no records state exactly what he found. From this he was able to summon the magic of the four elements, using magic as a tool and a weapon. He and
5	line	Wise Old Man	his followers learnt how to bind the power into little stones so that others could use it.
5	line	Wise Old Man	in the land south of here they constructed an immense tower where the power could be studied, but followers of Zamorak destroyed it with fire many years ago, and most of the knowledge was lost.
5	cond	If the player hasn't completed Rune Mysteries:
6	line	Wise Old Man	Perhaps one day those lost secrets will be uncovered once more.
6	action	continue
5	cond	If the player has completed Rune Mysteries:
6	line	Wise Old Man	I hear you've been very helpful to the wizards who are working on the mysteries of the rune stones.
6	line	Player	Well, I didn't do much...
6	action	continue
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
4	option	Settlements
5	line	Player	I suppose you'd know about the history of today's cities?
5	line	Wise Old Man	Yes, there are fairly good records of the formation of the cities from primitive settlements.
5	line	Wise Old Man	In the early part of the Fourth Age, of course, there were no permanent settlements. Tribes wandered the lands, staying where they could until the resources were exhausted.
5	line	Wise Old Man	This changed as people learnt to grow crops and breed animals, and now there are very few of the old nomadic tribes. There's at least one tribe roaming between the Troll Stronghold and Rellekka, though.
5	cond	If the player has completed Mountain Daughter:
6	line	Player	Yes, I've met them. They're all mad.
6	line	Wise Old Man	Truly, their faith in natural spirits is rather foolish, but they're a pleasant enough people.
6	action	continue
5	line	Wise Old Man	Anyway, what was I saying? Ah, yes...
5	line	Wise Old Man	One settlement was Avarrocka, a popular trading centre.
5	line	Wise Old Man	In the west, Ardougne gradually formed under the leadership of the Carnillean family, despite the threat of the Mahjarrat warlord Hazeel who dwelt in that area until his downfall.
5	cond	If the player sided with the cultists in Hazeel Cult:
6	line	Player	He'll be back, just you wait!
6	line	Wise Old Man	Oh dear, I hope you haven't done anything rash!
6	action	continue
5	cond	If the player sided with Ceril in Hazeel Cult:
6	line	Player	I've foiled a dastardly Zamorakian plot to have Hazeel resurrected.
6	line	Wise Old Man	So I'd heard. Lord Saradomin is smiling on you.
6	action	continue
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
4	option	The Wise Old Man of Draynor Village
5	line	Player	Tell me about yourself, old man.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Ah, so you want to know about me, eh?
5	line	Wise Old Man	Mmm... what could I say about myself? Let's see what I've done...
5	line	Wise Old Man	I've delved into the dungeon west of Brimhaven and heard the terrifying CRASH of the steel dragons battling each other for territory.
5	line	Wise Old Man	I spent some years on Entrana, where I learnt the techniques of pure meditation.
5	line	Wise Old Man	I've wandered through the vast desert that lies south of Al Kharid and seen the great walls of Menaphos and Sophanem.
5	cond	If the player has completed Icthlarin's Little Helper:
6	line	Player	That feline statue you've got on your bookshelf there - I'm sure I saw something like that when I was in Sophanem.
6	line	Wise Old Man	I've always liked to collect little trinkets to remind me of the time when my life was more - ah - exciting.
6	line	Player	So you've spoken to the Sphinx, then?
6	line	Wise Old Man	Spoken to a sphinx, you say? My dear young lady, you can't possibly be serious!
6	line	Player	What do you mean?
6	line	Wise Old Man	Ha ha ha! The people who live deep in the shifting sands of the desert will often tell travellers tall tales of strange beasts, but that doesn't mean any of it's remotely true!
6	line	Player	But I've met the Sph...
6	line	Wise Old Man	Please, adventurer, there is nothing to be gained by interfering in matters you do not understand.
6	line	Wise Old Man	Even if such a creature were to exist...
6	line	Player	... which it does...
6	line	Wise Old Man	EVEN IF SUCH A CREATURE WERE TO EXIST it would be terribly dangerous for you to get involved in its business.
6	line	Wise Old Man	I have heard of terrible things happening to travellers in that land, and I would not wish for you to be dragged into anything like that.
6	line	Wise Old Man	Indeed, I have heard of adventurers doing the most shameful and blasphemous deeds believing themselves to be acting on behalf of some false god!
6	line	Player	Hmmm?
6	line	Wise Old Man	So please do not speak to me of this matter again. Now, I believe I was telling you of my adventurous youth...
6	action	continue
5	line	Wise Old Man	Apart from all that, I've spent many a happy hour in dusty libraries, searching through ancient scrolls and texts for the wisdom of those who have passed on.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Plus plenty of other adventures, quests, journeys... Is there anything else you'd like to know?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
3	option	Gods and demons
4	option	Three gods?
5	line	Player	I heard that Gielinor has three gods.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Indeed. This is correct: Saradomin, Guthix and Zamorak.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Saradomin, the great and glorious, gives life to this world.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Zamorak craves only death and destruction.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Guthix, calling itself a god of 'balance', holds no allegiance, but simply aids whatever cause suits its shifting purpose.
5	cond	If the player has completed The Dig Site:
6	line	Player	So who's Zaros?
6	line	Wise Old Man	What did you say?
6	line	Player	I discovered a buried altar to a god called Zaros.
6	line	Wise Old Man	Please, do not speak further of this. No good can come of meddling in such things.
6	line	Player	So Zaros is real?
6	line	Wise Old Man	Adventurer, my patience is limited. Speak to me no further of this - this - this foolishness.
6	cond	If the player has completed Desert Treasure I:
7	line	Player	Does that mean I shouldn't ask you about the ancient magicks I learnt in that pyramid north of Sophanem?
7	line	Wise Old Man	ENOUGH! Begone from me, you foul trickster!
7	action	end
5	cond	If the player has completed Temple of Ikov but not Desert Treasure I:
6	line	Player	I've heard of another god, called Armadyl.
6	line	Wise Old Man	What is this of which you speak?
6	line	Player	A strange man asked me to go into the Temple of Ikov and steal the Staff of Armadyl.
6	line	Wise Old Man	And what makes you believe in this 'Armadyl'?
6	line	Player	Well, there were servants of Armadyl living down in the depths of the temple. They'd been there for generations, guarding the staff.
6	line	Wise Old Man	So you trusted the word of these people who had been sitting down a hole all their lives?
6	line	Player	Um... Yes, I suppose so.
6	line	Wise Old Man	I wouldn't worry about this sacred 'armadyllo' anymore. Just another foolish myth.
6	action	(If the player sided with the Guardians of Armadyl:)
7	line	Player	Oh well, the servants rewarded me very kindly for defeating Lucien for them.
7	line	Wise Old Man	That is an impressive feat, adventurer. Truly you must be beloved in the eyes of Saradomin.
6	action	(If the player sided with Lucien:)
7	line	Player	It's lucky there's no Armadyl! I've pinched his staff and given it to Lucien.
7	line	Wise Old Man	YOU'VE DONE WHAT?
7	line	Wise Old Man	Adventurer, I beg of you, do not meddle in the gods' affairs. No good can come of it.
6	action	If the player has completed Icthlarin's Little Helper but not Desert Treasure I:
6	line	Player	How about Tumeken, Elindis, Icthlarin and the Devourer?
6	line	Wise Old Man	What names are these?
6	line	Player	Down in Sophanem, they've got a chief god named Tumeken, plus a fertility goddess named Elindis. Icthlarin is their god of the dead and the Devourer...
6	line	Wise Old Man	Adventurer, what folly leads you to think any of these - things, exist?
6	line	Player	But I've met Icthlarin! He'd got a jackal's head!
6	line	Wise Old Man	It is hot in that land, and the heat can affect a traveller in strange ways. Tell me, when you met 'Icthlarin', had you been feeling at all unwell?
6	line	Player	Well, now you mention it, I'd just been hypnotised by a weird woman I met in the desert.
6	line	Wise Old Man	So a strange woman interfered with your mind, then you met a man with the head of a jackal, and you decided he must be a god?
6	line	Player	Umm...
6	line	Wise Old Man	Well, make sure you don't get hypnotised again, and I'm sure you'll not meet any more jackal-headed men claiming to be gods!
6	line	Player	But...?
6	line	Wise Old Man	It'd probably be best if you don't go there again.
6	line	Player	But you've been all around that area, haven't you? When you were travelling?
6	line	Wise Old Man	Indeed, I have.
6	line	Player	So you'd know all about their gods?
6	line	Wise Old Man	I know what I know.
6	line	Wise Old Man	And knowing what I know, I do not speak of this matter. Perhaps you would be wise to heed my example.
6	action	above
4	option	The wars of the gods
5	line	Player	I wanna know about the wars of the gods!
5	line	Wise Old Man	Ah, that was a terrible time. The armies of Saradomin fought gloriously against the minions of Zamorak, but many brave warriors and noble cities were overthrown and destroyed utterly.
5	cond	If the player has completed Shadow of the Storm:
6	line	Wise Old Man	You have visited Uzer, and seen for yourself the damage that could be wrought by an elder-demon in its wrath.
6	action	continue
5	line	Player	How did it all end?
5	line	Wise Old Man	Before the Zamorakian forces could be utterly routed, Lord Saradomin took pity on them and the battle- scarred world, and allowed a truce.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
4	option	The Mahjarrat
5	line	Player	What are the Mahjarrat?
5	line	Wise Old Man	Very little is written about the tribe of the Mahjarrat. They are believed to be from the realm of Freneskae, or Frenaskrae - the spelling in this tongue is only approximate.
5	line	Wise Old Man	One of them, the foul Zamorak, has achieved godhood, although none knows how this came about.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Other Mahjarrat who have been particularly active upon this plane are Hazeel, Lucien, Azzanadra and Zemouregal.
5	cond	If the player sided with the cultists in Hazeel Cult:
6	line	Player	Hazeel will rise again, you'll see!
6	line	Wise Old Man	Adventurer, your actions fill me with concern!
6	action	continue
5	cond	If the player sided with Ceril in Hazeel Cult:
6	line	Player	I've foiled a dastardly Zamorakian plot to have Hazeel resurrected.
6	line	Wise Old Man	So I'd heard. Lord Saradomin is smiling on you.
6	action	continue
5	cond	If the player sided with the Guardians of Armadyl in Temple of Ikov:
6	line	Player	I've defeated Lucien.
6	line	Wise Old Man	Truly, your bravery exceeds your stature. But I fear his defeat will not be permanent.
6	action	continue
5	cond	If the player sided with Lucien in Temple of Ikov:
6	line	Player	I've met Lucien. He paid me very nicely for bringing him a staff he wanted.
6	line	Wise Old Man	Traveller, I beg of you, do not have further dealings with such creatures! You do not know their power as I do.
6	action	continue
5	cond	If the player has completed Desert Treasure I:
6	line	Player	Azzanadra taught me some ancient magical powers after I unlocked the pyramid where he had been trapped.
6	line	Wise Old Man	Leave me, traveller; I am old, and your words fill me with horror.
5	action	end
4	option	Wielding the power of the gods
5	line	Player	Can I wield the power of Saradomin myself?
5	cond	If the player has completed Mage Arena I:
6	line	Wise Old Man	I see you are already learning to summon the power of Saradomin.
6	action	continue
5	cond	If the player hasn't completed Mage Arena I:
6	line	Wise Old Man	If you travel to the Mage Arena in the north-west reaches of the Wilderness, the battle mage Kolodion may be willing to let you learn to summon the power of Saradomin, should you be able to pass his test.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
3	option	Something to do with you...
4	option	Your hat!
5	line	Player	I want to ask you about your hat.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Why, thank you! I rather like it myself.
5	cond	If the player has not yet seen the recording of the Draynor Bank Robbery:
6	line	Player	Did you steal it from the bank?
6	line	Wise Old Man	Me? Steal from the bank? Whatever do you mean?
6	line	Player	There's been a break-in at Draynor Bank, and I bet you did it.
6	line	Wise Old Man	Oh my goodness, what in the world could make you think I did such a thing?
6	line	Player	Well, you've been sitting here looking at the bank ever since you moved into this house. Now someone's robbed the bank, and suddenly your house is full of expensive stuff!
6	line	Wise Old Man	Oh dear, oh dear...
6	line	Wise Old Man	So what do you think I did? March across the street, smash the bank wall, knock out the bankers and steal all the money?
6	line	Wise Old Man	I'm an old man! I walk with a stick! How could I possibly have done that?
6	line	Player	So you didn't rob the bank?
6	line	Wise Old Man	Just run along now, be a good lad, and don't worry yourself about me or my finances!
6	line	Player	Hmmm... But I'll be keeping an eye on you.
6	line	Wise Old Man	Now you've got that off your chest, would you like to ask me about anything else?
6	option	How can I get a hat like that?
7	action	below
6	option	Yes please.
7	action	above
5	cond	If the player has seen the recording of the Draynor Bank Robbery:
5	option	You stole it off that woman in the bank!
6	line	Player	You stole it off that woman in the bank! You stole all this valuable stuff too!
6	line	Wise Old Man	Stole it? How could you possibly think I did such a thing?
6	line	Player	I saw you robbing the bank! You killed all those people!
6	line	Wise Old Man	Deary me, {player}, your imagination is running wild! What could make you think you saw me do that?
6	line	Player	I've seen a security recording that shows you robbing the bank. The bank's guard showed it to me.
6	line	Wise Old Man	You've seen the bank's security recording?
6	line	Wise Old Man	Tut tut tut... Oh well, at least you'll never be able to tell the bank about me. They'll never listen.
6	line	Player	So you're just going to get away with it?
6	line	Wise Old Man	That's my plan, yes.
6	line	Player	But that's... well, it's WRONG!
6	line	Wise Old Man	Wrong? WRONG? I'll tell you what's wrong!
6	line	Wise Old Man	I've spent my whole life travelling the world, doing quests for people, saving lives, saving villages from terrifying monsters and all that sort of thing.
6	line	Wise Old Man	Now I'm old, and where do I have to live? In this freezing old house next to a pig-sty, with a bunch of yobs outside who can't keep their hands off the market stalls! What sort of reward is that?
6	line	Wise Old Man	So don't talk to me about right and wrong!
6	line	Player	Maybe someone SHOULD talk to you about right and wrong...
6	line	Wise Old Man	Bah!
6	line	Player	Hmmph!
6	line	Wise Old Man	Now you've got that off your chest, would you like to ask me about anything else?
6	option	How can I get a hat like that?
7	action	below
6	option	Yes please.
7	action	above
6	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
7	action	above
5	option	How can I get a hat like that?
6	line	Player	How can I get a hat like that?
6	line	Wise Old Man	You could buy one off another player, or wait until they're next made available by the Council.
6	line	Player	Can I buy your hat?
6	line	Wise Old Man	Ohhh no, I don't intend to part with this. Would you like to ask me about something else?
6	option	You should give it back, you know.
7	action	below
6	option	Yes please.
7	action	above
6	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
7	action	above
5	option	You should give it back, you know.
6	line	Player	You should give it back, you know.
6	line	Wise Old Man	No, I think I'll keep it.
6	line	Player	But...
6	line	Wise Old Man	Now you've got that off your chest, would you like to ask me about anything else?
6	option	How can I get a hat like that?
7	action	above
6	option	Yes please.
7	action	above
6	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
7	action	above
5	option	How can I get a hat like that?
6	action	above
4	option	That quest we did together...
5	line	Player	That was quite an exciting quest we did together!
5	line	Wise Old Man	Oh yes, it was certainly a fitting end to my adventuring days. Your fight against the Sea Troll Queen was highly impressive!
5	line	Player	Are you tempted to go on another quest in the future?
5	line	Wise Old Man	No, I feel I am a bit old for that kind of thing now. New times need new heroes, and I'm sure you'll always be there to answer the call!
5	line	Player	I'll certainly see what I can do!
5	line	Wise Old Man	Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
4	option	Your retirement
5	line	Player	When we finished fighting those sea trolls, you said you'd finished with adventuring, didn't you?
5	line	Wise Old Man	Yes, that's right. I'm an old man, there's no denying it, and I need a nice quiet retirement.
5	line	Wise Old Man	Besides, I think you've proved that the new generation has its own heroes and adventurers - I should step back and let you get on with it!
5	line	Player	Does this mean you're not going to do any more big robberies?
5	line	Wise Old Man	Well, since you saved my life when we were fighting the Sea Troll Queen, I don't mind telling you... I trust you won't tell anyone about this?
5	line	Player	Go on...
5	line	Wise Old Man	I might just have something in mind. After all, that little bank incident went very smoothly.
5	line	Player	But you're retired!
5	line	Wise Old Man	I retired from adventuring and questing. The episode in the bank was hardly a quest, more like a shopping trip!
5	line	Player	Your shopping trip killed 3 bank staff and several innocent bystanders, not to mention the watchman!
5	line	Wise Old Man	I've saved countless villages from unspeakable terrors and slain innumerable evil monsters - surely I deserve some sort of reward in return? Yet what did I get? NOTHING!
5	line	Wise Old Man	You yourself would get pretty angry if you did a long and dangerous quest and didn't get any reward from it, eh? I'm sure you would!
5	line	Wise Old Man	Well imagine how I felt at the end of a long life of questing when was left penniless, and I had to move into this thief-infested village! This little shack was falling apart when I arrived!
5	line	Wise Old Man	You go speak to that hag who keeps looking through my window - she'll show you how it used to look before I could afford to redecorate it!
5	line	Wise Old Man	Being noble and virtuous simply doesn't put food on the table, and I don't intend to sit in banks begging like so many people do these days.
5	line	Player	So all those quests in the past, when you saved people from monsters and stuff like that... You only helped them because you wanted a reward?
5	line	Wise Old Man	No, it wasn't always like that. I used to be satisfied just knowing that I'd helped, and that was reward enough.
5	line	Wise Old Man	But eventually I realised that people forgot about me as soon as the danger was gone, and I wasn't even getting paid properly for my services. Sometimes they offered training in the various skills, but that's no use to me!
5	line	Wise Old Man	I eventually realised that the only way I could get a proper reward for my life's efforts is if I took the reward myself. So I took up my cape and staff and headed for the bank.
5	line	Player	And now you're planning to do another robbery? Didn't you get enough from the bank?
5	line	Wise Old Man	Perhaps not... But enough of this matter! Is there anything else you'd like to ask?
5	option	Yes please.
6	action	above
5	option	Thanks, maybe some other time.
6	action	above
